{"id":"h2-07-a2","title":"gRPC, GraphQL and when to choose each","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: gRPC and protobuf internals, GraphQL schema and N+1, comparison with REST, decision guide, load balancing and compatibility. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"the-problem-how-do-two-programs-talk","title":"The problem: how do two programs talk?","html":"<p><strong>An API style is a contract for how a client asks and a server answers.</strong> REST, gRPC and GraphQL are three different contracts. None is \"best\"; each fixes a different pain.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>REST:</strong> many URLs, one per resource; JSON; works everywhere including browsers.</li>\n<li><strong>gRPC:</strong> you call functions on a remote server (<code>GetUser(id)</code>); binary Protocol Buffers over HTTP/2; strongly typed.</li>\n<li><strong>GraphQL:</strong> one URL; the client writes a query describing exactly the fields it wants.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 649.6 192\" width=\"649.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three ways a client can fetch a user and their orders\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M491.6 34 L547.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M491.6 34 L547.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M491.6 96 L547.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M491.6 96 L547.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M491.6 158 L547.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M491.6 158 L547.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"333.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"324.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">REST: GET /users/7 then GET /users/7/orders</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"333.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"324.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">gRPC: GetUserWithOrders</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"333.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"324.8\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">GraphQL: one query with chosen fields</text><rect x=\"547.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"592.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Server</text></svg><figcaption>Three ways a client can fetch a user and their orders</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A profile screen needs name, avatar, last 3 orders. REST: 2 round trips (say 80 ms each on mobile = 160 ms) and over-fetching of unused fields. GraphQL: 1 round trip with only the needed fields. gRPC: 1 call, but the shape is fixed by the service.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google invented gRPC (from internal Stubby). Facebook invented GraphQL (2012, open sourced 2015) because the News Feed mobile app was drowning in REST round trips. Stripe and GitHub (REST v3) chose REST for broad public reach; GitHub also offers GraphQL v4.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Ordering food: REST is a set menu with separate counters, gRPC is a phone line to the kitchen with a fixed order form, GraphQL is \"I will describe exactly what I want on my plate\".</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answering \"GraphQL replaces REST\". It does not; they solve different problems.</li>\n<li>Not asking who the clients are (public browsers vs internal services) before choosing.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"grpc-internals","title":"gRPC internals","html":"<p><strong>gRPC = Protocol Buffers (a compact binary format) + HTTP/2 + generated client/server code.</strong></p>\n<p>You write a <code>.proto</code> file; a compiler generates Kotlin/Java/Go/etc. stubs.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span># user.proto</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>syntax = \"proto3\";</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>service UserService {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  rpc GetUser (GetUserRequest) returns (User);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  rpc ListOrders (ListOrdersRequest) returns (stream Order);   // server streaming</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  rpc Chat (stream Msg) returns (stream Msg);                  // bidirectional</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>message GetUserRequest { int64 id = 1; }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>message User { int64 id = 1; string name = 2; string email = 3; }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Key facts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Field numbers</strong> (<code>= 1</code>) are the identity on the wire, not names. Never reuse or renumber; mark removed ones <code>reserved</code>. That is how backward compatibility works.</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP/2:</strong> multiplexes many calls on one TCP connection, header compression (HPACK), binary framing. No head-of-line blocking at the HTTP layer (TCP-level blocking remains).</li>\n<li><strong>Four call types:</strong> unary, server streaming, client streaming, bidirectional streaming.</li>\n<li><strong>Deadlines:</strong> the client sets a timeout that propagates through the whole call chain; services stop work when it expires. Always set one.</li>\n<li><strong>Status codes:</strong> gRPC has its own (<code>OK</code>, <code>NOT_FOUND</code>, <code>INVALID_ARGUMENT</code>, <code>UNAVAILABLE</code>, <code>DEADLINE_EXCEEDED</code>, <code>UNAUTHENTICATED</code>, <code>PERMISSION_DENIED</code>...), not HTTP codes.</li>\n<li><strong>Size:</strong> protobuf is typically 3 to 10x smaller than the equivalent JSON and faster to parse (varint encoding: small numbers take 1 byte).</li>\n<li><strong>Metadata</strong> (headers) carries auth tokens and trace ids; <strong>interceptors</strong> handle logging, auth, retries.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 503.2 192\" width=\"503.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One TCP connection carries many concurrent calls\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M332 34 L388 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M332 34 L388 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Android app</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">HTTP/2 connection</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">stream 1 GetUser</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"251.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">stream 3 ListOrders</text><rect x=\"388\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"439.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">gRPC server</text></svg><figcaption>One TCP connection carries many concurrent calls</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> JSON user <code>{\"id\":123456,\"name\":\"Asha\",\"email\":\"a@x.com\"}</code> is about 50 bytes. Protobuf: id as varint (3 bytes + 1 tag), name (1 + 1 + 4), email (1 + 1 + 8), about 20 bytes. At 50,000 calls/s between internal services that saves roughly 1.5 MB/s plus CPU on parsing.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google (everything internal), Netflix (moved many inter-service calls to gRPC), Square, Uber, Dropbox (gRPC replaced custom RPC), etcd and Kubernetes components (kube-apiserver to etcd), Envoy xDS.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A typed form with numbered boxes: both sides agree box 1 is the id, so nobody needs to write the word \"id\" each time.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reusing a protobuf field number with a different meaning (silent data corruption).</li>\n<li>No deadlines: one slow dependency piles up threads everywhere.</li>\n<li>Browsers cannot speak native gRPC (no control of HTTP/2 framing); use gRPC-Web with a proxy (Envoy).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"grpc-in-production-load-balancing-and-compatibility","title":"gRPC in production: load balancing and compatibility","html":"<p><strong>Because gRPC keeps one long-lived HTTP/2 connection, a plain L4 load balancer sends all of a client's calls to one backend.</strong> This is the classic gRPC incident: one pod at 95% CPU, others idle after scaling out.</p>\n<p>Fixes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>L7 balancer</strong> that understands HTTP/2 streams (Envoy, Linkerd, Istio, NGINX with grpc_pass, AWS ALB gRPC).</li>\n<li><strong>Client-side load balancing:</strong> client gets all backend addresses (DNS or xDS) and round-robins per call (<code>round_robin</code> policy).</li>\n<li><strong>Max connection age</strong> on servers (for example 5 min with grace) so connections rotate and new pods get traffic.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compatibility rules for protobuf evolution:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Adding a field: safe (old readers ignore it).</li>\n<li>Removing a field: reserve its number and name.</li>\n<li>Changing a type: mostly breaking (int32 to int64 is wire-compatible, int to string is not).</li>\n<li>New enum values: old clients see them as the default/unknown; always handle <code>UNRECOGNIZED</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Try a gRPC service from the terminal</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">grpcurl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -plaintext</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> '{\"id\": 7}'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> localhost:9090</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> UserService/GetUser</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 419.2 192\" width=\"419.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Per-call balancing needs L7 or client-side logic\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Envoy proxy</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Pod A</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Pod B</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Pod C</text></svg><figcaption>Per-call balancing needs L7 or client-side logic</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Retries:</strong> gRPC supports a retry policy via service config (for example 3 attempts, backoff 0.1 s to 1 s, on <code>UNAVAILABLE</code>). Retry only idempotent methods.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Kubernetes + Istio users hit this exact imbalance after enabling gRPC; Lyft built Envoy largely for this kind of L7 balancing.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A taxi dispatcher who sends every call from one company to the same driver because \"they already have a ride in progress\".</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming a Kubernetes ClusterIP Service balances gRPC well (it balances connections, not calls).</li>\n<li>Retrying non-idempotent RPCs automatically.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"graphql-internals","title":"GraphQL internals","html":"<p><strong>GraphQL is a query language plus a typed schema; the client asks for exactly the fields it needs from a single endpoint (usually <code>POST /graphql</code>).</strong></p>\n<p>Schema (the contract):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>type User { id: ID!  name: String!  orders(first: Int): [Order!]! }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>type Order { id: ID!  total: Int!  items: [Item!]! }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>type Query { user(id: ID!): User }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>type Mutation { cancelOrder(id: ID!): Order }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>type Subscription { orderUpdated(id: ID!): Order }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>(<code>!</code> means non-null.)</p>\n<p>Query:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>query {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  user(id: \"7\") { name  orders(first: 3) { id total } }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Response mirrors the query shape exactly, so no over-fetching and no under-fetching.</p>\n<p>How the server runs it: each field has a <strong>resolver</strong> function. The engine walks the query tree calling resolvers. Three operation types: <strong>query</strong> (read), <strong>mutation</strong> (write, run serially), <strong>subscription</strong> (push over WebSocket/SSE).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 802.4000000000001 130\" width=\"802.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One query fans out to many resolvers\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M456.40000000000003 65 L512.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M456.40000000000003 65 L512.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M644.4000000000001 34 L700.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M644.4000000000001 34 L700.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M456.40000000000003 65 L512.4000000000001 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M456.40000000000003 65 L512.4000000000001 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M644.4000000000001 96 L700.4000000000001 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M644.4000000000001 96 L700.4000000000001 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">POST /graphql</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">GraphQL server</text><rect x=\"512.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"578.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">User resolver</text><rect x=\"512.4000000000001\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"578.4000000000001\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orders resolver</text><rect x=\"700.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"745.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users DB</text><rect x=\"700.4000000000001\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"745.4000000000001\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orders DB</text></svg><figcaption>One query fans out to many resolvers</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>The N+1 problem.</strong> Query 50 users, each with orders: 1 query for users + 50 queries for orders = 51 DB calls. Fix with <strong>DataLoader</strong> (batching): collect all 50 user ids in one tick, run one <code>WHERE user_id IN (...)</code>. Result: 2 queries.</p>\n<p><strong>Other real issues:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Query cost / depth attacks:</strong> a client can ask <code>user { friends { friends { friends ... } } }</code>. Defend with max depth (for example 8), query cost scoring, timeouts, and persisted queries (allow-list of hashes).</li>\n<li><strong>Caching:</strong> everything is POST to one URL, so HTTP/CDN caching is lost; use persisted queries via GET, response caching per field, or Apollo client normalized cache.</li>\n<li><strong>Errors:</strong> HTTP 200 with an <code>errors</code> array is normal, so monitoring must look inside the body.</li>\n<li><strong>File upload, rate limiting by cost</strong> are extra work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Mobile home screen via REST: <code>/me</code>, <code>/feed</code>, <code>/notifications</code>, <code>/ads</code> = 4 calls, 30 KB. GraphQL: 1 call, 9 KB selecting only displayed fields. On 150 ms RTT networks that is roughly 450 ms saved.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Facebook (origin), GitHub v4 API, Shopify Storefront API, Netflix (federated GraphQL gateway over microservices), Airbnb and Apollo Federation (a gateway stitching many teams' subgraphs).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A buffet where you tell the server exactly which items and how much; no pre-packed meal with stuff you throw away.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignoring N+1 (it is the first follow-up question).</li>\n<li>Forgetting authorization must be on each resolver/field, not just the endpoint.</li>\n<li>Exposing introspection and unlimited depth on a public production API.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"head-to-head-comparison","title":"Head-to-head comparison","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>REST</th>\n<th>gRPC</th>\n<th>GraphQL</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Transport</td>\n<td>HTTP/1.1 or 2</td>\n<td>HTTP/2</td>\n<td>HTTP (usually POST)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Format</td>\n<td>JSON (text)</td>\n<td>Protobuf (binary)</td>\n<td>JSON</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contract</td>\n<td>OpenAPI (optional)</td>\n<td><code>.proto</code> (mandatory)</td>\n<td>Schema (mandatory)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Typing</td>\n<td>Weak unless OpenAPI</td>\n<td>Strong, generated</td>\n<td>Strong, introspectable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Streaming</td>\n<td>SSE/WebSocket add-ons</td>\n<td>Native, 4 modes</td>\n<td>Subscriptions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Browser support</td>\n<td>Native</td>\n<td>Needs gRPC-Web</td>\n<td>Native</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>HTTP caching</td>\n<td>Excellent</td>\n<td>Poor</td>\n<td>Poor (needs work)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Payload size</td>\n<td>Medium</td>\n<td>Smallest</td>\n<td>Exactly what you ask</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Over/under fetching</td>\n<td>Common</td>\n<td>Fixed by RPC shape</td>\n<td>Solved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Learning curve</td>\n<td>Lowest</td>\n<td>Medium</td>\n<td>Medium to high</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Debugging</td>\n<td>curl, browser</td>\n<td>grpcurl, needs tooling</td>\n<td>GraphiQL, needs tooling</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Versioning</td>\n<td>URL/headers</td>\n<td>Add fields, reserve</td>\n<td>Deprecate fields</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Performance rule of thumb: gRPC is often 2 to 7x faster than REST/JSON for small messages internally, mostly from serialization and connection reuse. Confirm with your own benchmark; numbers vary.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 553.6 130\" width=\"553.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Typical modern layout\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M108 96 L164 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 96 L164 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M324.8 96 L380.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M324.8 96 L380.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Mobile app</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Partner</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"244.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">GraphQL BFF gateway</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"244.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">REST public API</text><rect x=\"380.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"461.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">gRPC Orders service</text><rect x=\"380.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"461.20000000000005\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">gRPC Users service</text></svg><figcaption>Typical modern layout</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> This exact layout (public REST or GraphQL at the edge, gRPC inside) is common at Netflix, Uber and Square.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Letters (REST: readable by anyone), a private radio code (gRPC: compact and fast but both sides need the codebook), a custom order form (GraphQL).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Picking one style for everything. Mixing by layer is normal.</li>\n<li>Quoting benchmark numbers as facts without caveats.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"when-to-choose-which","title":"When to choose which","html":"<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The API style is a <strong>one-way door</strong> for external clients (they cannot easily migrate) and a <strong>two-way door</strong> for internal ones (you control both ends).</p>\n<p>Choose <strong>REST</strong> when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Public or partner API; broad tooling; browsers and curl must work.</li>\n<li>Resources map cleanly to nouns; caching (CDN, ETag) matters.</li>\n<li>Team is small, you want the least surprise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choose <strong>gRPC</strong> when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Internal service-to-service, polyglot (Java, Go, Python), high QPS, low latency.</li>\n<li>You need streaming (telemetry, chat, large downloads in chunks).</li>\n<li>You want generated clients and enforced contracts in CI.</li>\n<li>Mobile apps can use gRPC too (battery and bandwidth savings), at the cost of proxy and debugging complexity.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choose <strong>GraphQL</strong> when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Many different clients (iOS, Android, web, TV) need different shapes of the same data.</li>\n<li>Mobile on poor networks where round trips hurt.</li>\n<li>Many backend services aggregated by one gateway (BFF).</li>\n<li>You accept the cost: N+1 control, cost limiting, harder caching.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Alternatives and when each breaks:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>REST breaks when screens need 5+ calls or APIs sprout <code>?include=</code>, <code>?fields=</code> hacks. Fix: BFF or GraphQL.</li>\n<li>gRPC breaks for public web clients and when ops teams lack HTTP/2-aware proxies.</li>\n<li>GraphQL breaks when the API is simple CRUD (you pay complexity for nothing) or traffic is heavily cacheable.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 612.4 192\" width=\"612.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A quick decision path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M454.4 34 L510.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M454.4 34 L510.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M454.4 96 L510.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M454.4 96 L510.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M165.6 96 L221.6 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M454.4 158 L510.4 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M454.4 158 L510.4 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"88.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Who is the client?</text><rect x=\"221.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"232.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Public/browser</text><rect x=\"221.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"232.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Internal services</text><rect x=\"221.6\" y=\"136\" width=\"232.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Many screens, flexible shapes</text><rect x=\"510.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"555.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">REST</text><rect x=\"510.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"555.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">gRPC</text><rect x=\"510.4\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"555.4\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">GraphQL</text></svg><figcaption>A quick decision path</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Ride-hailing: driver location updates at 1 per 4 s from 500,000 drivers = 125,000 updates/s. A bidirectional gRPC stream per driver (small protobuf, about 30 bytes of payload) is far cheaper than 125,000 REST POSTs/s each with 500+ bytes of headers. Rider-facing \"trip history\" is REST or GraphQL.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber internal services use gRPC/Thrift-style RPC. Shopify exposes both REST and GraphQL and pushes new features GraphQL-first. Twitter's internal Finagle/Thrift similarly.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Choosing between a bus (REST, goes anywhere, everyone can board), a private metro line (gRPC, fast but fixed stations), and a taxi you instruct stop by stop (GraphQL).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not stating the client mix and QPS before recommending.</li>\n<li>Forgetting migration: you can front an existing REST service with a GraphQL gateway without rewriting it.</li>\n<li>Treating \"newer\" as \"better\".</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"other-options-worth-knowing","title":"Other options worth knowing","html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Thrift</strong> (Facebook/Apache): like gRPC, older, own transport options.</li>\n<li><strong>tRPC / JSON-RPC:</strong> typed RPC over HTTP+JSON; fine for TypeScript monorepos.</li>\n<li><strong>WebSockets / SSE:</strong> for pushing data, not a request/response style (see the real-time note).</li>\n<li><strong>OpenAPI</strong> (Swagger): describes REST APIs so you can generate clients (Retrofit interfaces) and docs. Gives REST some of gRPC's contract benefits.</li>\n<li><strong>Webhooks:</strong> the server calls <em>your</em> URL when something happens; used by Stripe, GitHub.</li>\n<li><strong>Kafka/queues:</strong> asynchronous messaging when you do not need an immediate reply.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 474.40000000000003 68\" width=\"474.40000000000003\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Async alternative: do not wait for the answer\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Order service</text><rect x=\"185.60000000000002\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.20000000000002\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka topic</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"403.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Email service</text></svg><figcaption>Async alternative: do not wait for the answer</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Phone call (sync RPC) vs sending a letter (queue): choose by whether you must wait for the answer.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using synchronous calls for everything, then suffering cascading failures when one service is slow.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>REST: resource URLs plus JSON, universal and cacheable; best for public APIs.</li>\n<li>gRPC: protobuf over HTTP/2, typed, streaming, fast; best for internal service-to-service. Never reuse field numbers, always set deadlines, balance per call (L7 or client-side).</li>\n<li>GraphQL: one endpoint, client picks fields; fixes over/under-fetching for diverse clients. Watch N+1 (DataLoader), query depth/cost, caching, per-field authorization.</li>\n<li>Common production layout: GraphQL or REST at the edge, gRPC inside.</li>\n<li>Choose based on clients, QPS, streaming needs, team skills and caching; edge APIs are one-way doors, internal ones are not.</li>\n<li>Know the failure modes: gRPC imbalance behind L4, GraphQL N+1 and depth attacks, REST chatty round trips.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}